  {:id :LOOP-RELOAD-UNMAP-013 :status :active :supersedes :AGENT-PROBE-RELOAD-017
   :ears "When a warm check reloads the dependency closure of its targets (every namespace of the closure, dependencies before dependents, with require :reload), then after each namespace reloads and before any dependent reloads, the runner shall ns-unmap exactly the vars interned in that namespace that its file used to define (their :file metadata names the namespace's file) and that this evaluation of the file did not define (their metadata map is the object recorded before the reload), and list each in the receipt's unmapped (ns, var, former file:line). It shall never remove-ns a namespace of the closure: defonce state and the identity of every var the file still defines (functions, protocols, multimethods) survive. Vars without :file metadata (runtime interns, stubs) and vars another file defined shall be kept. A failed reload shall unmap nothing. The supported probe shall continue to unload (remove-ns) and reload its named target namespaces through tools.namespace, so deleted test vars cannot survive as stale red or green."
   :misreadings ["require :reload removes definitions the file no longer has." "remove-ns is the same repair with fewer steps." "A var still interned after a reload is still defined by the file." "Unmapping breaks compiled callers that hold the var." "Reloading named namespaces attests all loaded dependencies."]
   :boundaries ["Deleted defn" "Deleted deftest in a source dependency" "defonce state" "Protocol and record still defined" "Runtime intern without :file" "Var defined by another file" "Failed reload" "Dependent that still refers the deleted var (fails to load, as cold)" "Probe target namespaces (remove-ns, unchanged)" "Deleted red Var" "Deleted green Var"]
   :tests [:a-definition-deleted-from-its-file-is-unmapped-and-defonce-state-survives :only-vars-the-file-defined-are-unmapped
           :deleted-test-vars-do-not-survive-probes]
   :rationale "Item 1 of the reload-correctness batch, 2026-10-31: AGENT-PROBE-RELOAD-017 promised unloading, which only the probe's own target namespaces got (image/reload-probe!, tools.namespace remove-ns); every source namespace check! reloaded kept deleted definitions alive, a false green. Owner-approved target: unmap exactly what the file no longer defines, never remove-ns (keeps defonce state and protocol/record var identity)."}
  {:id :LOOP-STALE-REFER-011 :status :active
   :ears "After a warm check's reload loop succeeds, the runner shall compare the declared refers (the ns form, including :refer :all, :use, :only and :rename) of each reloaded namespace that could have silently refused one (a namespace in which the reload unmapped or kept a stale definition, per LOOP-RELOAD-UNMAP-013, or that Clojure named in a REJECTED line) with its actual mappings, and shall sweep every loaded namespace for mappings to a var the reload unmapped. When a declared refer does not map to the var its home namespace now exports, or a namespace maps a var its home's file no longer defines, the receipt shall report status fail, stage stale-image, jvm-usable true, a stale map (refers, referrers with in-closure?, defs with their former file:line, the captured REJECTED and WARNING reload lines, check-ms), and one failures entry of kind stale per stale mapping naming the namespace, symbol, actual and expected var and the repair; it shall never report pass. Clojure's reload stderr shall still reach stderr. Stale definitions with no referrer shall be listed (and a stderr line printed) without changing the verdict. A local definition the file still has, shadowing a declared refer, is not stale (a cold JVM ends the same way)."
   :misreadings ["require :reload removes definitions the file no longer has." "A warm green on namespace X attests namespaces that refer X." "Clojure's REJECTED line on the runner's stderr is a report." "Comparing ns-interns before and after a reload finds deleted vars." "A stale image is an unknown that needs a cold start." "Every refer shadowed by a local defn is stale."]
   :boundaries ["Function moved, old namespace refers it (REJECTED)" "Function deleted, referrer outside the closure" "Function deleted, nobody refers it" ":refer :all and :use" ":rename" "Prefix lists" "Local defn shadowing a refer" "Runtime intern without :file" "Home not yet reloaded (order)" "Deleted test var (unmapped by LOOP-RELOAD-UNMAP-013)" "Older runner without jvm-usable"]
   :tests [:a-refused-refer-after-a-move-is-reported-and-never-a-pass
           :a-referrer-outside-the-closure-holding-a-stale-var-is-named-with-in-closure-false
           :an-unreferenced-stale-definition-warns-and-keeps-the-verdict
